<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    The claim action inside the XP card, and the one button in this app that
    is allowed to shout.

    Solid gold where bg_button_stars_outline is deliberately outlined. That
    file's own note explains why the outline is normally right - filled, gold
    is the loudest thing on the screen by a wide margin - and this is the case
    that wants exactly that. It is only ever on screen while stars are owed
    and unclaimed, which is the one state on the level card the player can act
    on and the one they lose by ignoring. The moment the queue empties, the
    button goes back to bg_button_xp_outline and the card is quiet again.

    Same 10dp radius as both outlined buttons, so swapping between them does
    not change the shape of the card.
-->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:state_pressed="true">
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="@color/gold_deep" />
            <corners android:radius="10dp" />
        </shape>
    </item>
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="@color/stars_accent" />
            <corners android:radius="10dp" />
        </shape>
    </item>
</selector>
